---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import "@styles/demo.css";
---

<Base
	title="Live demos"
	description="Live demos of systems by John-Franklin Anusiem: a Rust USSD framework, a Go media-storage library and a multi-agent runtime with a multiplayer tabletop game."
>
	<div class="demo">
		<section class="wrap demo-intro" data-cloud="orb">
			<p class="eyebrow"><b>Live</b> · try the real thing</p>
			<h1>Three systems, four demos. Poke at them.</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				These aren't recordings or mock-ups. Each page talks to the actual library running on a small
				server, behind the same setup I'd use in production. Break something, then tell me what happened.
				There's a feedback form at the bottom of every page.
			</p>
			<div id="api-status"></div>
		</section>

		<section class="wrap demo-body">
			<div class="cards">
				<a class="card" href="/demo/ussd">
					<div class="card-top"><span class="chip">Rust</span><span class="chip">ussdframework</span></div>
					<h2>Dial a loan</h2>
					<p>A phone you can dial <code>*384#</code> on, backed by my Rust USSD framework. Borrow, repay,
						fail a PIN, then rewrite the menu JSON and dial again to watch your changes run.</p>
					<span class="go">Open the phone →</span>
				</a>
				<a class="card" href="/demo/buckt">
					<div class="card-top"><span class="chip">Go</span><span class="chip">buckt</span></div>
					<h2>A media sandbox</h2>
					<p>Your own private bucket for an hour. Upload images and see thumbnails generated, send the
						same file twice and see it stored once, trash and restore, and watch lifecycle events fire.</p>
					<span class="go">Open the sandbox →</span>
				</a>
				<a class="card" href="/demo/loom">
					<div class="card-top"><span class="chip">Go</span><span class="chip">loom</span></div>
					<h2>Run a table with agents</h2>
					<p>Host a multiplayer tabletop game: write the world, share a code, and let an AI run it or run
						it yourself with AI-voiced NPCs. Every round shows what each agent cost. Or rewire an agent pipeline.</p>
					<span class="go">Open the runtime →</span>
				</a>
				<a class="card" href="/demo/forecast">
					<div class="card-top"><span class="chip">Go</span><span class="chip">loom</span></div>
					<h2>The Forecast Desk</h2>
					<p>A fictional league with play chips. Forecast matches against a value hunter and a contrarian whose
						stakes a bankroll agent sizes and a hook polices, rewind any matchday, and backtest the strategies.</p>
					<span class="go">Open the desk →</span>
				</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section id="feedback"></section>
	</div>
</Base>

<script>
	import { mountFeedback, checkApi, $ } from "../../scripts/demo/common.js";
	mountFeedback("general");
	checkApi($("#api-status"));
</script>
